e, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] [17592186105368 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040017/assets/26d09b87ebbabe4c1e1dcd8d5442b1d3efce216d7f404808a3777b8ffa3304ff.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}({x}^{2}+1),\\, & -1<x\\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^1 f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x = 1$\n\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function"] [17592186105377 :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{3}+k{x}^{2},\\, & 0<x<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186102122 17592186102123 17592186102124 17592186102125 17592186102126 17592186102128 17592186102129 17592186102130 17592186102131 17592186102132 17592186105258 17592186105259 17592186105260 17592186105261 17592186105262 17592186105348 17592186105349 17592186105350 17592186105351 17592186105352 17592186305034 17592186305035 17592186305036 17592186305037 17592186305038 17592186305041 17592186305042 17592186305043 17592186305044 17592186305045 17592186305055 17592186305056 17592186305057 17592186305058 17592186305059 17592186305090 17592186305091 17592186305092 17592186305093 17592186305094] "immutable_fields" [[17592186102121 :answer-field/correct] [17592186102121 :answer-field/id] [17592186102121 :answer-field/key] [17592186102121 :answer-field/type] [17592186102127 :answer-field/correct] [17592186102127 :answer-field/id] [17592186102127 :answer-field/key] [17592186102127 :answer-field/type] [17592186105257 :answer-field/correct] [17592186105257 :answer-field/id] [17592186105257 :answer-field/key] [17592186105257 :answer-field/type] [17592186105347 :answer-field/correct] [17592186105347 :answer